WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.950
As we mention in our body systems intro video from many years ago- there are some misconceptions.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.978
Human blood is red and always red although the shade of

00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:13.950
red can vary based on how much oxygen is in the blood.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.836
Veins and arteries are often drawn in diagrams as blue or

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:22.677
red to show whether they have lower or higher concentrations of oxygen,

00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:25.950
but that’s just how it is used in most diagrams.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.950
It doesn’t mean the blood, or the veins, or arteries are actually that color.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.862
Veins that you see under your skin may look blue or green by the way,

00:00:34.912 --> 00:00:38.264
but that involves the way they appear under the skin and the

00:00:38.314 --> 00:00:41.950
reason for this would make a great physics topic — but I digress.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.468
Human blood has a lot of functions.

00:00:44.518 --> 00:00:48.497
It maintains a certain pH, temperature, osmotic pressure

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:51.950
– all of this is very important for homeostasis.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.021
It transports things like hormones, nutrients, and gases.

00:00:56.071 --> 00:00:58.950
And it’s made up of different components.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.011
One component includes plasma, the liquid portion.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:07.950
Water, proteins, salts, lipids- you’ll find them in this liquid portion of blood known as plasma.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.514
Another component includes cellular components.

00:01:10.564 --> 00:01:13.950
This means red blood cells, which do the transporting of gases.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.950
White blood cells which can fight infections.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.109
And platelets, which are actually cellular fragments,

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:23.089
and they’re involved with helping your blood clot.

00:01:23.139 --> 00:01:25.950
Very important when there is damage to the body.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.737
Red blood cells have an iron-containing protein called hemoglobin,

00:01:29.787 --> 00:01:32.950
and that is where that red coloring of blood comes from.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.747
So, when we’re talking about blood, and we’re just introing the circulatory system,

00:01:36.797 --> 00:01:39.950
we’re going to focus on how this blood moves around in the human body.
